{"id": "github_site|docs/resources/explanations/Issue_2025_1_Column_Applicability.md|3", "text": "ResStock 2025 Release 1 Column Applicability — Issue Report: ResStock 2025 Release 1 Column Applicability > Details

applied in upgrade 01, Natural Gas Furnace 95% AFUE. One additional column, **upgrade.hvac_detailed_performance_data**, was only correctly applied in upgrade 04, Cold Climate Air-Source Heat Pump.

**upgrade.heating_fuel**, as noted in the [enumeration dictionary](https://oedi-data-lake.s3.amazonaws.com/nrel-pds-building-stock/end-use-load-profiles-for-us-building-stock/2025/resstock_amy2018_release_1/enumeration_dictionary.tsv) for this release, only has two potential values: “Natural Gas” and “None”. That means for other upgrades that are electric, such as the single-speed geothermal heat pump, their **upgrade.heating_fuel** is marked as “None” even though the final upgraded heating fuel is in fact electric for example. Similarly, the **upgrade.hvac_heating_type_and_fuel** only has two potential values, “Natural Gas Fuel Furnace” and “None”. Even if a model gets a change of heating system that is not a natural gas furnace, the column will show up as “None”. To fix this, infer the type of upgrade from other columns and ResStock documentation. For example, upgrade 02 in this dataset is the Propane Furnace 95% AFUE or Fuel Oil Furnace 88% AFUE. Looking at the **applicability** column and the **in.heating_fuel** column in the <ins>annual results files</ins> gives the needed information. Also check the dataset [readme](https://oedi-data-lake.s3.amazonaws.com/nrel-pds-building-stock/end-use-load-profiles-for-us-building-stock/2025/resstock_amy2018_release_1/README_resstock_20251.pdf) for a summary of applicability logic, or the upgrade specific documentation if it is released", "metadata": {"product": "resstock", "release": "resstock_amy2018_2025_release_1", "source_id": "github_site", "source_type": "markdown", "source_path": "docs/resources/explanations/Issue_2025_1_Column_Applicability.md", "doc_title": "ResStock 2025 Release 1 Column Applicability", "section": "Issue Report: ResStock 2025 Release 1 Column Applicability > Details", "line_start": 18, "line_end": 18, "corpus_version": "resstock_amy2018_2025_release_1-v1", "status": "site_page", "date_last_updated": "2026-01-20", "date_last_updated_source": "git_commit"}}
{"id": "github_site|docs/resources/explanations/Issue_2025_1_Column_Applicability.md|4", "text": "ResStock 2025 Release 1 Column Applicability — Issue Report: ResStock 2025 Release 1 Column Applicability > Details

for a summary of applicability logic, or the upgrade specific documentation if it is released

. For example, say the **applicability** column is marked as “True” and the **in.heating_fuel** column value is “Propane”, then a user can infer the upgrade was applied and actual value of the **upgrade.heating_fuel** should be “Propane”, and the **upgrade.hvac_heating_type_and_fuel** should be “Propane Fuel Furnace”. From the readme, the user knows that less efficient propane systems are upgraded only with the propane system, they are not upgraded with the fuel oil system. This is one example of how the actual value can be inferred.

**upgrade.hvac_detailed_performance_data**, also noted in the [enumeration dictionary](https://oedi-data-lake.s3.amazonaws.com/nrel-pds-building-stock/end-use-load-profiles-for-us-building-stock/2025/resstock_amy2018_release_1/enumeration_dictionary.tsv) for this release, only has two potential values, “Cold Climate Heat Pump Ducted” and “None”. To find out the efficiency of other hvac systems in different upgrades, check out the **upgrade.hvac_heating_efficiency** column or the **upgrade.hvac_cooling_efficiency** column which will have the hvac system type and efficiency value.", "metadata": {"product": "resstock", "release": "resstock_amy2018_2025_release_1", "source_id": "github_site", "source_type": "markdown", "source_path": "docs/resources/explanations/Issue_2025_1_Column_Applicability.md", "doc_title": "ResStock 2025 Release 1 Column Applicability", "section": "Issue Report: ResStock 2025 Release 1 Column Applicability > Details", "line_start": 18, "line_end": 20, "corpus_version": "resstock_amy2018_2025_release_1-v1", "status": "site_page", "date_last_updated": "2026-01-20", "date_last_updated_source": "git_commit"}}

